{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlposition"]}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL11MXLPositionV","symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","title":"MXLPosition","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPosition"}],"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPosition"}]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"changed two ways."}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"]]},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPosition"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default-x and default-y attributes change the computation of the default position. For most elements, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"origin is changed relative to the left-hand side of the note or the musical position within the bar (x) and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the top line of the staff (y)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For the following elements, the default-x value changes the origin relative to the start of the current"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"measure:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"note - figured-bass - harmony - link - directive - measure-numbering - all descendants of the part-list"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element - all children of the direction-type element"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This origin is from the start of the entire measure, at either the left barline or the start of the system."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the default-x attribute is used within a child element of the part-name-display, part-abbreviation-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"display, group-name-display, or group-abbreviation-display elements, it changes the origin relative to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"start of the first measure on the system. These values are used when the current measure or a succeeding"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"measure starts a new system. The same change of origin is used for the group-symbol element."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For the note, figured-bass, and harmony elements, the default-x value is considered to have adjusted the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"musical position within the bar for its descendant elements."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Since the credit-words and credit-image elements are not related to a measure, in these cases the default-x"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and default-y attributes adjust the origin relative to the bottom left-hand corner of the specified page."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The relative-x and relative-y attributes change the position relative to the default position, either as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"computed by the individual program, or as overridden by the default-x and default-y attributes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Positive x is right, negative x is left; positive y is up, negative y is down. All units are in tenths of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interline space. For stems, positive relative-y lengthens a stem while negative relative-y shortens it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default-x and default-y position attributes provide higher-resolution positioning data than related"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"features such as the placement attribute and the offset element. Applications reading a MusicXML file that can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"understand both features should generally rely on the default-x and default-y attributes for their greater"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accuracy. For the relative-x and relative-y attributes, the offset element, placement attribute, and directive"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute provide context for the relative position information, so the two features should be interpreted"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"together."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"As elsewhere in the MusicXML format, tenths are the global tenths defined by the scaling element, not the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"local tenths of a staff resized by the staff-size element."}]}]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/init(defaultX:defaultY:relativeX:relativeY:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/defaultX","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/defaultY","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/relativeX","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/relativeY"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/Equatable-Implementations"],"anchor":"Defau